movie trailers in general are often  guilty of lying to us and it seems that  goes double for Star Wars the rise of  Skywalker trailers have made us believe  we're going to see a number of things  that probably won't happen here's a look  at some of the biggest mr. X one of the  most surprising shots and the rise of  Skywalker marketing comes from the  second trailer which was released at the  d23 Expo in August we're talking about  the shot of Rey in a hooded cloak  holding a lightsaber with two red beams  we've never seen a lightsaber like that  in a Star Wars movie so it's an  intriguing reveal on its own but then it  unfolds into a double-ended weapon  reminiscent of Darth Maul's  clearly this shot is meant to make you  wonder if Rey will follow up on our  darkside temptations and go evil for the  end of the trilogy but no one really  thinks that's going to happen right  especially after the marketing team for  the last Jedi did kind of the exact same  thing already  I don't believe that a couple  explanations come to mind the first is  that Rey is having a dream or vision  like Luke did during his visit to  Dagobah in the Empire Strikes Back  another possibility is that the dark  version of Rey is some kind of evil  clone we don't know for sure but it  seems the least likely option is that  the shining beacon of hope will turn  evil and stay that way in the final  installment of her trilogy also seen in  the second rise of Skywalker trailer is  a brief but curious shot of everyone's  trusty and perpetually anxious protocol  droid c-3po with conspicuously red eyes  the big implication here is that somehow  c-3po has been tampered with in some way  the droids red eyes are a first in his  skywalker saga arc and they seem to  imply that some entity has infiltrated  c-3po why else would they go red punch  three shooters c-3po red eyes seem like  a misdirect intended to mislead viewers  by encouraging them to think that the  Droid has turned to the dark side  is it a temporary malfunction maybe a  simple problem with some faulty wiring  our favorite golden droid isn't getting  any younger so it's not surprising that  he might need a tune-up or upgrade for  years on but the red eyes somehow  indicating c-3po is going to become a  tool for the dark side is probably one  idea we should definitely drop the final  trailer for the rise of Skywalker  features a shot of Rey and kylo Ren  fighting side-by-side considering that  plenty of other footage shows them  fighting each other it's tough to gauge  what the rise of Skywalker wants us to  believe about these characters we've  already seen Rey and kylo Ren work  together to defeat Snoke and his guards  in the last Jedi they've also shared a  connection through their force  sensitivities even communicating and  tracking one another's movements it  would be easy to think the Skywalker  saga was gearing up to make some  grandiose statement about finding and  embracing the gray area between the  light and dark sides of the force and  teaming up with your presumed enemy  against a far bigger threat on the other  hand Rey and kylo Ren returned to their  respective teams after defeating Snoke  in the last Jedi and remained enemies  through the end of the film by showing  us scenes of them fighting against and  alongside each other it's clear they  don't want us to know what actually  happens the big question that comes from  the shot of Rey and kylo Ren teaming up  in the trailer is why they're doing it  in the first place  is there a mutual recognition of their  power and capabilities are they really  teaming up or just trying to exploit  each other to keep all that a mystery  the marketing is trying to have it both  ways  Ray's back story has been a mystery for  Star Wars fans ever since episode 7  first came out years ago she's  essentially the main character of Star  Wars right now and we really don't know  a lot about her past or present other  than the fact that she's really really  good at using the force very few clues  have been dropped about her life before  we meet her in the force awakens to date  all we know is that she was abandoned on  the planet jakku which led her to a life  of scavenging believing she was nobody  through interrogations intense  conversations kylo  has frequently hinted that he knows the  truth about Rey's past including her  parents who were apparently no one  special  filthy junk traders who sold her for  drinking money you have no place in my  story you come from nothing you're  nothing  knowing this makes one particular moment  in the rise of Skywalker trailers all  the more intriguing during the final  trailer as they face off in the rain on  a piece of wreckage Rey is seen looking  at kylo Ren while her voiceover states  nobody knows me the camera cuts  revealing kylo Ren as he activates his  lightsaber and his voiceover replies but  I do putting these two shots and their  corresponding voiceover one after the  other in the final trailer certainly  implies kylo Ren will reveal Rey's past  or some other potentially  earth-shattering truth about her that  will change her direction in the rise of  Skywalker it's the kind of tease that  gives you deja vu  haven't we already dealt with this issue  was kylo lying before or are the  trailers lying now furthermore does  anyone even care who raised family is at  this point  it wasn't Luke it wasn't leia and it  wasn't han and it's probably not Lando  this late in the game would a big reveal  about her parentage even matter it's  probably Palpatine isn't it maybe that's  how we get evil Rey why not this is  where the fun begins check out one of  our newest videos right here plus even  more looper videos about Star Wars are  coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]
 

